    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Show, using substitution, that $G(-9,-12)$ lies on the circle centred at the origin with radius 15.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(-9)^2+(-12)^2=81+144=225=15^2$, so $G$ lies on the circle.",
      "worked": "The circle has equation $x^2+y^2=225$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(-9)^2+(-12)^2&=81+144\\\\(-9)^2+(-12)^2&=225\\end{align*}$$\nThe coordinates satisfy the equation, so $G$ lies on the circle.",
